        role: "Highway Patrol trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What happened in the construction zone on {DATE}?", "\"A tractor-trailer driven by {D} rear-ended {V}'s car, killing {V}. I responded as the trooper.\""), .direct("What did {DL}'s breath test show?", "\"A .11. That's over the legal limit. I administered the test at the scene.\""), .direct("What does the truck camera show?", "\"No braking until impact. The truck drove into the back of {V}'s car without slowing.\""), .direct("What did you see on arrival at the crash?", "\"A tractor-trailer wedged against a car that had been crushed against a barrier. {V} was trapped in the driver's seat and died at about 4:40.\""), .direct("How did the truck camera help?", "\"It shows the road ahead and the speed. The truck held steady until impact, with no braking and no steering to avoid the car.\""), .direct("What did you smell or see in the cab?", "\"A smell of alcohol on {D.his} breath, bloodshot eyes, and slow speech. I asked for a breath test and {D.he} agreed.\""), .cross("{DL} says traffic stopped suddenly, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Traffic does slow in construction zones. But a truck should be ready for that.\""), .cross("Were warning signs posted?", "\"Yes. There were signs. Whether they were early enough is something I can't speak to.\""), .cross("Was {V}'s car stopped?", "\"It was slowed or stopped in traffic. I'm not able to say precisely how.\""), .cross("Were warning signs posted far enough ahead?", "\"There were signs about a half mile before the work zone, with a lane closure and reduced speed ahead. I did not measure their timing.\""), .cross("Was the traffic in front of the truck stopped?", "\"It had slowed to a crawl. {V}'s car was waiting in line, and the truck came upon it.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Highway worker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you work in the zone?", "\"Yes. I'm a highway worker. I'm in that zone daily.\""), .direct("Were the signs adequate?", "\"Late, in my opinion. They were placed close to the work area. Drivers had little warning.\""), .direct("Does traffic stop quickly there?", "\"Often. It backs up fast. It can catch a driver off guard.\""), .direct("What is your job in the work zone?", "\"I help set cones and signs and direct traffic during lane closures. I have worked on that stretch for three years.\""), .direct("How far out were the first warning signs?", "\"About half a mile. Some drivers said it was too close for a heavy truck at speed.\""), .direct("How does traffic usually behave there?", "\"It flows fine until it hits the merge, then it stops suddenly. It catches a lot of drivers off guard.\""), .cross("Were signs posted?", "\"Yes. They were posted. I'm not saying they weren't there.\""), .cross("Could a sober driver see them?", "\"I'd think so. Most drivers do. It's a hazard we all know.\""), .cross("Were you there at the crash?", "\"No. I arrived afterward. I only know the zone.\""), .cross("Were you present when the crash happened?", "\"No. I came after the call. I helped with cones and traffic control.\""), .cross("Would a sober, attentive driver be able to stop in time?", "\"Most would. But it takes full attention, which is why we put out signs.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove drunk and killed.", "A sudden stop."),
        allocution: "\"I'll never forgive myself.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a bottle in the cab.", "Signs were placed only a half mile out."),
        defendant: [.direct("What happened in the construction zone?", "\"Traffic stopped fast. I tried to brake, but I was too close. I didn't see the slowdown in time.\""), .direct("Had you been drinking?", "\"I'd had a drink earlier. I didn't think I was impaired. I feel terrible about it.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I'm devastated. I think about {V} and the family every day.\""), .direct("How long have you driven trucks?", "\"Twenty years. I know the routes and the rules, and my record is mostly clean.\""), .direct("What was the traffic like as you came toward the work zone?", "\"Free-flowing and then it suddenly bunched up. I saw brake lights late and felt the truck settle forward when I stepped on the pedal.\""), .direct("Deputies said they smelled alcohol on you. Had you been drinking?", "\"I had a drink earlier that day, and I will not deny it. I did not think I was impaired when I got behind the wheel.\""), .cross("The camera shows no braking until impact, doesn't it?", "\"That's what they say. I braked late. I was caught off guard.\""), .cross("You blew a .11, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I'm not going to argue the number. I regret it deeply.\""), .cross("The construction signs were posted, weren't they?", "\"They were. I saw them late. I should have slowed sooner.\""), .cross("You blew .11 and did not brake until impact. Isn't it obvious you were impaired?", "\"I know the number. I will not say I was perfect, but I braked as soon as I saw what was ahead.\""), .cross("You are a professional driver. Why not slow when you saw signs?", "\"I did slow some. I should have slowed more. I live with that.\"")],
        openings: ("In a construction zone, a tractor-trailer driven by {D} rear-ended {V}'s car and killed {V}. {D} blew a .11, and the truck camera shows no braking until impact. The State will present the trooper.", "The defense will present a zone where traffic stopped suddenly, warning signs that came late, and a driver who is devastated. Listen closely to the witnesses."),
        closings: ("A .11 breath test, no braking until impact, and the smell of alcohol in the cab of a tractor-trailer. {V} was stopped in line, doing nothing wrong, and did not survive the collision.", "Signs came late, traffic stopped suddenly, and a truck cannot stop on a dime. The State must prove that impairment, not a sudden stop, caused this death, and the evidence leaves room for doubt."),
        timeline: [(0, "4 p.m.: construction zone."), (0, "4:20 p.m.: impact."), (0, "4:40 p.m.: {V} dies."), (0, "5 p.m.: breath test.")],
        identified: "A breath test.",
        aggravating: [],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
