        role: "Highway Patrol trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What does the intersection camera show?", "\"Two cars racing away from a red light. One of them jumped a curb and struck {V} on a sidewalk.\""), .direct("What did your crash report find about speed?", "\"The car that hit {V} was going 80 miles an hour in a 35 zone. That is more than double the limit.\""), .direct("Who drove that car?", "\"{D}. {V} died from the injuries, as the autopsy confirms.\""), .direct("What does the video show before the light changed?", "\"Two cars side by side in the left and center lanes at a red light. Engines can be heard revving, and both launch the instant the cross traffic clears.\""), .direct("How did the crash happen?", "\"The car in the left lane, driven by {DL}, veered across the right lane and jumped the curb. It struck {V} on the sidewalk about a block past the intersection.\""), .direct("What did you measure at the scene?", "\"A tire mark of more than a hundred feet, a curb gouge, and a point of impact about forty feet onto the sidewalk. The speed estimate was about 80 in a 35.\""), .cross("{D} says the other car cut {D.him} off, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. The other driver turned in front of {DL}'s car. The video shows a turn.\""), .cross("Did the defendant rev the engine at the light?", "\"Yes. The camera shows the engine being revved. I will say that.\""), .cross("Were both cars racing?", "\"They both accelerated hard. I cannot say it was an agreed race.\""), .cross("Did the other car stop?", "\"No. It kept driving for a few blocks and then pulled over when the driver heard sirens. That driver was interviewed and released.\""), .cross("Did the other driver turn in front of the defendant's car?", "\"The video shows the other car moving right as it crossed the intersection, which could have cut into {D.his} path. I cannot say it forced {D.him} onto the curb.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Other driver",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you cut {D} off at the light?", "\"I turned in front of {D}'s car. I did not mean to cut anyone off. I was turning.\""), .direct("Were you racing the defendant?", "\"No. I was not racing. I was driving through the intersection and turned.\""), .direct("How fast were you going?", "\"Normal. Not fast. I was turning, not speeding.\""), .direct("Where were you headed that night?", "\"Home from a late shift. I was in the right lane at the light, ready to turn right once it changed.\""), .direct("What did the defendant's car do when the light changed?", "\"It roared off. I started my turn and saw headlights coming up behind me very fast.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I braked and finished the turn. I heard the crash a few seconds later and stopped when I saw the lights in my mirror.\""), .cross("Did you hear the defendant rev the engine?", "\"Yes. I heard it. I did not take it as a challenge.\""), .cross("Did you accelerate hard from the light?", "\"I accelerated with traffic. I would not call it hard.\""), .cross("Did you see the crash?", "\"I saw it in my mirror. I stopped when I realized.\""), .cross("Did you accelerate with the defendant?", "\"I moved forward when the light changed, like everyone. I was not trying to keep pace with anybody.\""), .cross("How close did your car come to {D}'s?", "\"I would say a couple of car lengths. I never touched it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} raced and killed.", "A cut-off."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} revved at the light.", "The other driver turned in front."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you racing?", "\"No. I was not racing anyone. I was reacting to a car that turned in front of me.\""), .direct("How fast were you going?", "\"Fast. I do not know exactly. I sped up to avoid the other car.\""), .direct("Did you rev your engine at the light?", "\"Yes. I did. It was a habit. I did not mean it as a challenge.\""), .direct("What do you remember of the intersection that night?", "\"A red light, a car next to me, and a lot of noise. I was heading home from work with the windows down and the radio loud.\""), .direct("What happened when the light turned green?", "\"I hit the gas to get through. The other car moved right across my lane, and I swerved to avoid it. Then I felt the curb.\""), .direct("What did you do after the crash?", "\"I stopped, got out, and ran to {V}. I called 911 and stayed with {V.him} until the medics came.\""), .cross("80 in a 35, wasn't it?", "\"That is what the report says. I was not watching the speedometer.\""), .cross("Someone is dead because of how you drove, isn't that right?", "\"Yes. I am heartbroken. I did not mean for this.\""), .cross("You revved at the light and accelerated hard. How is that not racing?", "\"I did not agree to race. I reacted.\""), .cross("You said you did not agree to race. Why did you rev your engine?", "\"It is a bad habit. I do it at lights without thinking. I know it looks like a challenge.\""), .cross("Eighty miles an hour in a 35 is not a reaction. Isn't it a choice?", "\"I was not watching my speed. I accelerated hard to get away from the other car, and that was a wrong choice.\"")],
        openings: ("Two cars raced from a red light, and one jumped a curb at 80 miles an hour in a 35 zone, killing {V} on a sidewalk. {D} drove that car and revved at the light.", "The defense evidence will establish that another car turned in front of {D}, that there was no agreed race, and that {D} reacted without thinking."),
        closings: ("Two cars, a revved engine, 80 miles an hour in a 35 zone, and {V} dead on a sidewalk. {D} chose the speed that killed, and that choice has consequences.", "A car that turned in front of {D}, a sudden reaction, and a terrible result. The State must prove {D} agreed to race, and a revved engine is not an agreement."),
