        role: "Safety inspector",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the site after the fall?", "\"{V}, a laborer, had fallen from a scaffold and died. No harness was provided to workers on the site that day.\""), .direct("What is {D}'s history with your office?", "\"{D}, the contractor, had been cited twice before for safety violations. One citation carried a $1,200 fine.\""), .direct("What did a coworker tell you?", "\"That there were no harnesses on site. The coworker said it plainly when I interviewed the crew.\""), .direct("What did you find at the scaffold site?", "\"A three-story scaffold with missing guardrails on one side and no tie-off anchors. {V}'s body was on the ground below the north corner.\""), .direct("What safety gear was on site?", "\"Hard hats and gloves for most of the crew. No harnesses were issued, and there was no lanyard attached to any anchor.\""), .direct("What did the defendant's prior citations involve?", "\"Two earlier visits found missing guardrails and inadequate fall protection. {D.He} paid fines and promised to fix the problems.\""), .cross("{D} says {V} refused equipment, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, {DL} says that. A harness was found in {DL}'s truck, which I will acknowledge.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} refuse a harness?", "\"No. I did not see it. I only know what the crew and {DL} told me.\""), .cross("Whose responsibility is it to make sure a harness is worn?", "\"The employer's. The employer must provide equipment and enforce its use, no matter what a worker prefers.\""), .cross("Did you find a harness in the defendant's truck?", "\"Yes, one. It was in a toolbox in the truck bed. I cannot say when it was put there.\""), .cross("Did the defendant cooperate with the investigation?", "\"Yes. {D.He} gave us the crew list and answered our questions without objection.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Coworker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {V} refuse a harness?", "\"Yes, {V} waved it off when it was offered. I saw it, and I remember because {V} said it slowed the work.\""), .direct("How many times was a harness offered to {V}?", "\"Once that I saw. {D} held one up, and {V} waved it away without much thought.\""), .direct("Was {V} experienced on scaffolds?", "\"Yes, {V} had worked scaffolds for years and felt comfortable up there. That is why the refusal did not worry anyone.\""), .direct("How long have you worked with {D} and {V}?", "\"Three years with {DF}, and a year with {V}. We worked side by side on most jobs.\""), .direct("What did you see that morning?", "\"{D.He} showed {V} a harness, and {V} waved it away. Then {V} climbed the ladder to the third level.\""), .direct("How would you describe {V} on scaffolds?", "\"Confident. {V} moved fast and often skipped steps. A few of us teased {V} about it.\""), .cross("Did the defendant insist that {V} put the harness on?", "\"Not that I saw. {DF} offered it once and let {V} go up without it.\""), .cross("Were harnesses available for the other workers on site?", "\"I do not think so. I did not see more than one, and it was kept in {D.his} truck.\""), .cross("Had you been told to use harnesses at that site?", "\"Not clearly. It was not a rule that anyone enforced on that crew.\""), .cross("Did the defendant stop {V} from going up?", "\"No. {DF} asked once and let {V} go. I did not hear any order to put it on.\""), .cross("Were there any rules about harnesses on the crew?", "\"Not firm ones. We were told to be careful, but no one enforced a harness policy.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} skipped safety gear.", "A refusal."),
        allocution: "\"I'll live with it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been fined $1,200.", "A harness was in {DL}'s truck."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you leave your workers without safety gear?", "\"No. I had a harness available, and I offered it. I did not send anyone up without the option.\""), .direct("What did {V} do when you offered it?", "\"{V} refused. {V} waved it off and said it was not needed, and I did not force the issue.\""), .direct("Where was the harness kept?", "\"In my truck, which was parked at the site. I brought it out when I saw {V} heading up.\""), .direct("What kind of crew did you have that day?", "\"Six people building a three-story frame. {V} had worked scaffolds for years and often went up first.\""), .direct("Tell the jury about the harness.", "\"I had one in my truck. I took it out and held it up to {V}, who waved it off and went up anyway.\""), .direct("What did you do when {V} fell?", "\"I ran to the corner, saw {V} was not breathing, and called 911. I told the deputies everything and showed them the harness.\""), .cross("You had been cited twice before and fined $1,200, hadn't you?", "\"Yes. I know my record. I tried to do better, and I thought I was following the rules this time.\""), .cross("One harness for a whole crew. Is that enough?", "\"It was not enough, and I know it. I should have had more equipment on site.\""), .cross("A worker is dead because no one made {V.him} wear a harness, isn't that right?", "\"{V} is on my mind from the moment I wake up. I should have insisted. I did not, and that is on me.\""), .cross("One harness for six workers is not a safety program. Do you agree?", "\"I agree. I should have had one for every worker and a plan for using them.\""), .cross("You could have refused to let {V} go up. Why didn't you?", "\"I did not insist. I was behind schedule, and I did not want to argue with an experienced worker.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, a laborer, fell from a scaffold and died. No harnesses were on site for the crew, and {D}, the contractor, had already been cited twice for safety violations.", "Weigh the defense proof, which will show that {D} offered a harness, that {V} waved it off, and that {D} did not know {V} would go up without one."),
        closings: ("A scaffold, no harnesses for the crew, two prior citations, and a worker who is dead. The employer is responsible for safety, and {D} did not provide it.", "A harness in the truck, offered once, and waved off by an experienced worker. The State must prove {D} acted with reckless disregard, and an offered harness cuts against that."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The second citation."), (0, "10 a.m.: the fall."), (0, "10:05 a.m.: medics."), (0, "11 a.m.: {V} dies.")],
        identified: "Safety citations.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "He had three kids.",
        doctrines: ["lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["V": .male])

    static let dogsKillChild = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.dogsKillChild",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Owner Kept Vicious Dogs That Killed a Neighbor's Child", "Fence Gate Left Open"],
        law: "invManslaughter",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Unintentionally killed {V} without malice through culpable negligence, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Two dogs killed {V}, a six-year-old, on {DATE} after the gate of {D}'s yard was left open. The dogs had attacked before. {DL} says a stranger opened the gate.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Animal Control Records", "Two prior attacks."), E(.statement, 3, "Neighbor", "'The gate was open.'"), E(.forensic, 2, "Autopsy", "Fatal injuries.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stranger", "{DL} says a stranger opened the gate.")],
        role: "Animal control officer",
        exam: [.direct("What do your animal control records show about {DL}'s dogs?", "\"Two prior attacks. The dogs had a history, and {D} knew about it.\""), .direct("What happened to {V}?", "\"Two dogs killed {V}, a six-year-old, after the gate of {DL}'s yard was left open. The autopsy found fatal injuries.\""), .direct("What did a neighbor tell you?", "\"That the gate was open. The neighbor saw it, and that's in the statement.\""), .direct("What were the two earlier attacks?", "\"One involved a delivery worker bitten on the leg two years before, and the other a neighbor's dog injured last spring. Both were documented, and both led to written notices.\""), .direct("What did the notices require of {D}?", "\"Secure fencing, a latched gate, and keeping the dogs inside or on a leash when anyone was near. Each notice carried {D.his} signature.\""), .direct("What did you see when you arrived after the 911 call?", "\"Two large dogs standing over {V} in the yard next to {DL}'s fence. The gate was swinging open, and a neighbor was holding the dogs back with a rake.\""), .cross("{DL} says a stranger opened the gate, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I have no witness to a stranger. I can only tell you the gate was open.\""), .cross("Was the gate latched earlier?", "\"A delivery driver says it was latched at noon. I can't say about later.\""), .cross("Did {DL} cooperate with you?", "\"Yes. {D.He} answered questions and showed me the yard.\""), .cross("How many people had keys or access to the gate latch?", "\"It had a simple hook latch with no lock. Anyone who lifted it could open it.\""), .cross("Did the defendant follow the earlier notices?", "\"In part. {D.He} had put up a taller fence after the second incident, but the latch was never upgraded.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Delivery driver",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you deliver to {DL}'s house?", "\"Yes. I'm a delivery driver. I came by around noon.\""), .direct("Was the gate latched?", "\"At noon, yes. I latched it myself after leaving a package.\""), .direct("Did you see the dogs?", "\"I heard them. They were inside the yard, behind the gate.\""), .direct("What route do you drive?", "\"A delivery route through this neighborhood. I stop at the same houses most days, and I know most of the dogs.\""), .direct("What did you do at {D}'s gate at noon?", "\"I left a package on the porch, stepped back through the gate, and dropped the latch. I always do that when there are dogs inside.\""), .direct("How did the dogs act when you came?", "\"They barked and jumped along the fence but did not get out. I kept my eyes on them as I closed the gate.\""), .cross("Was it latched at 3?", "\"Unknown. I wasn't there at 3. I can only speak to noon.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone else at the gate?", "\"No. No one. I left after the delivery.\""), .cross("Could the gate have been opened after you left?", "\"Of course. Anyone could have. I can't say who.\""), .cross("Did you tell the defendant the gate was latched?", "\"No. I did not talk to anyone. I left the package and drove on.\""), .cross("How can you be sure it stayed latched after you left?", "\"I cannot. I only know it was latched when I left, which was around noon.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kept dangerous dogs.", "A stranger opened the gate."),
        allocution: "\"I'm so sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been told to keep them muzzled.", "A delivery driver says the gate was latched at noon."),
        defendant: [.direct("How did the gate come to be open?", "\"A stranger opened it. I had it latched. Someone must have come into the yard.\""), .direct("Did you know the dogs had attacked before?", "\"Yes. I knew. I kept them in the yard to keep them away from people.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"I can't sleep. A child died because of my dogs. I'd do anything to change it.\""), .direct("How long have you owned the dogs?", "\"Five years. I got them as puppies and kept them in the yard. They were family to me.\""), .direct("What did you do after the earlier attacks?", "\"I added height to the fence and put up a sign. I told myself the gate latch was enough.\""), .direct("Where were you when it happened?", "\"Inside the house on the phone. I heard barking and screaming, ran outside, and found the gate open.\""), .cross("The dogs had two prior attacks, didn't they?", "\"Yes. That's why I kept the gate shut. I thought it was secure.\""), .cross("The gate was open when {V} was attacked, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. That's what the neighbor says. I don't know how.\""), .cross("You can't name the stranger, can you?", "\"No. I never saw anyone. I know that makes it sound like I'm blaming someone else.\""), .cross("Two prior attacks and only a hook on the gate. Is that responsible?", "\"No. I should have put a lock on it and a second gate. I did not do enough.\""), .cross("Why do you think a stranger opened it and not a child wandering in?", "\"I do not know who opened it. I only know I latched it that morning, and I never saw anyone at the gate.\"")],
        openings: ("Two dogs with two prior attacks killed {V}, a six-year-old, after the gate to {D}'s yard was left open. The State will show the animal control records, the neighbor, and the autopsy.", "The defense will present a gate that was latched at noon, a driver who confirms it, and a stranger who must have opened it. Listen closely to the witnesses."),
        closings: ("Two dogs known to attack, a gate left open, and a child dead. {D} knew the danger and failed to secure it.", "The gate was latched at noon and no one knows who opened it. The State has not proved {D} left it open."),
        timeline: [(-90, "The second attack."), (0, "Noon: gate latched, driver says."), (0, "3 p.m.: the attack."), (0, "3:30 p.m.: {V} dies.")],
        identified: "Animal records.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was particularly vulnerable"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "She was playing in her yard.",
        doctrines: ["lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["V": .female])

    static let kennelFireAnimals = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.kennelFireAnimals",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Kennel Burned With Animals Inside, Owner Charged", "Insurance Raised Weeks Earlier"],
        law: "burningBuildings",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Willfully and maliciously burned a kennel owned by {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A kennel burned overnight on {DATE}, killing eleven dogs. {D}, the owner, had raised the insurance weeks earlier. Investigators found two ignition points. {DL} says wiring failed.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Fire Report", "Two ignition points."), E(.document, 3, "Policy Change", "Coverage raised 40%."), E(.video, 2, "Road Camera", "{D}'s truck leaves at midnight.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Wiring", "{DL} says wiring failed.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the kennel on {DATE}?", "\"It burned overnight, killing eleven dogs. I found two ignition points.\""), .direct("What does the insurance record show?", "\"{D} raised the coverage by 40 percent a few weeks before the fire. The policy change is in evidence.\""), .direct("What does the road camera show?", "\"{D.his} truck leaving at midnight. The fire was discovered after that.\""), .direct("How did the fire spread through the building?", "\"It started in the middle aisle and in the back office area at nearly the same time, then raced along the ceiling through the runs. Within twenty minutes the roof collapsed.\""), .direct("What did you find at the two ignition points?", "\"Heavy charring at the floor in each location and no common electrical source between them. A lab found traces of an ignitable liquid in one.\""), .direct("What did the insurance paperwork say?", "\"Coverage was raised by forty percent about six weeks before the fire, with a larger payout for contents and animals.\""), .cross("{DL} says wiring failed, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Wiring can cause fires. But two separate ignition points are unusual for one fault.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} start the fire?", "\"No. No one did. This is a circumstantial case.\""), .cross("Was there faulty wiring in the building?", "\"I saw some wiring issues. I don't know that they started the fire.\""), .cross("How old was the wiring?", "\"The building dated to the seventies. The panel had been replaced once, and I saw some older runs in the attic.\""), .cross("Did you rule out all electrical causes?", "\"I ruled out the main panel, but I could not examine every circuit because the roof collapsed.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Electrician",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you work on the kennel's wiring?", "\"Yes. I'm an electrician. I inspected the kennel in the spring.\""), .direct("Did you note faults?", "\"Yes. I noted several wiring faults and told {D}.\""), .direct("Were they in this building?", "\"Yes. In this building. They were real problems.\""), .direct("How long have you been an electrician?", "\"Twenty-two years. I wire houses and small commercial buildings, and I inspect older structures.\""), .direct("What did you find at the kennel in the spring?", "\"Frayed insulation in the attic, scorch marks at two outlets, and an overloaded breaker feeding the back runs.\""), .direct("What did you tell {D}?", "\"That the building needed a rewire and that parts of it were a hazard. I gave a rough estimate of a few thousand dollars.\""), .cross("Could the faults cause a fire?", "\"They could. I can't say they did. I wasn't there.\""), .cross("Did {DL} fix them?", "\"I don't know. I wasn't asked to do repairs.\""), .cross("Can faults cause two ignition points?", "\"Unusual. I'd expect one. I can't say.\""), .cross("Did the defendant hire you to fix it?", "\"No. I gave the quote, and {D.he} said to wait. I did not hear back.\""), .cross("Could the faults you saw cause two separate fires?", "\"Possible, if two circuits failed at once. It would be unlikely.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned a kennel.", "Faulty wiring."),
        allocution: "\"I'm so sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} owed $60,000.", "An electrician noted wiring faults in the spring."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you burn your kennel?", "\"No. Those dogs were in my care. I'd never put them in danger.\""), .direct("Why did you raise the insurance?", "\"My agent recommended it. I had expanded and needed more coverage. It was routine.\""), .direct("What do you think caused the fire?", "\"Wiring. The building was old and the electrical work wasn't great. I'd worried about it.\""), .direct("Why did you open the kennel?", "\"I love dogs, and I built it over eight years. I boarded a dozen at a time and trained a few. It was my whole life.\""), .direct("What was the state of the building?", "\"Old and drafty. Breakers tripped in the summer, and I was told the wiring needed work. I put off the expense.\""), .direct("What did you do when you heard about the fire?", "\"I raced there. It was already burning, and the crews would not let me in. I screamed for the dogs.\""), .cross("You raised coverage weeks before the fire, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. It was a coincidence. I'm devastated.\""), .cross("Eleven dogs died, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I loved them. I feel awful.\""), .cross("Your truck left at midnight, didn't it?", "\"Yes. I went home as usual. The fire came later.\""), .cross("You raised your coverage, you owed money, and your truck left at midnight. Doesn't that look like arson?", "\"It looks like a bad coincidence. I raised coverage because my agent said I was underinsured.\""), .cross("Two fires in one building, forty minutes apart. How would wiring do that?", "\"I do not know. I am not an expert. I only know I did not start either one.\"")],
        openings: ("A kennel burned overnight, killing eleven dogs. Investigators found two ignition points, {D} had raised coverage weeks earlier, and {D}'s truck left at midnight. The State will present the fire marshal.", "Jurors will also see old wiring that an electrician flagged months earlier, an owner who loved those dogs, and no one who saw a fire set."),
        closings: ("Two ignition points, coverage raised by 40 percent, and a truck leaving at midnight. Eleven dogs died, and the evidence points to {D}.", "Faulty wiring was flagged in the spring, and no one saw {D} start a fire. The State has not proved the fire was set."),
        timeline: [(-21, "Coverage raised."), (0, "Midnight: {DL} leaves."), (0, "2 a.m.: the fire."), (0, "3 a.m.: crews.")],
        identified: "A fire report.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "They were family pets.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let warehouseInventoryBurn = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.warehouseInventoryBurn",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Warehouse Burned for Inventory Insurance, Investigators Say", "Sprinklers Disabled"],
        law: "burningBuildings",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Willfully and maliciously burned a warehouse owned by {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A warehouse burned on {DATE} with sprinklers shut off. {D}, a tenant, had removed stock days earlier. {DL} says a contractor shut the sprinklers.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Fire Report", "Accelerant near the pallets."), E(.document, 3, "Inventory", "Stock moved out days earlier."), E(.document, 2, "Sprinkler Log", "Valve closed at 6 p.m.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Contractor", "{DL} says a contractor closed the valve.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("What did your investigation find about the warehouse fire?", "\"Accelerant near the pallets, according to the fire report. The sprinklers were shut off when the fire started.\""), .direct("What did the sprinkler log show?", "\"The valve was closed at 6 p.m. That means the sprinklers could not work when the fire started later that night.\""), .direct("What did the inventory show about {D}'s stock?", "\"{D}, a tenant, had moved stock out of the warehouse days earlier. The inventory records show it.\""), .direct("What were the conditions when crews arrived?", "\"The warehouse was fully involved, with flames venting through the roof. Sprinklers were dry because the main control valve had been shut.\""), .direct("What did you find at the point of origin?", "\"A pattern of heavy burning along the north wall near stacked pallets, with an ignitable liquid residue in the debris.\""), .direct("What can you tell about the stock the tenant had moved?", "\"Records show most of the high-value inventory was shipped out a few days before. What remained was low-value packaging and empty pallets.\""), .cross("{D} says a contractor closed the sprinkler valve, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. The contractor's invoice mentions testing the sprinklers, and I will agree that testing could explain a closed valve.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} set the fire?", "\"No. No one saw {D.him} do it. We have the fire report, the log, and the inventory.\""), .cross("Is moving stock out unusual for a tenant?", "\"Not by itself. Tenants move stock all the time, but the timing matters here.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant at the warehouse the night of the fire?", "\"No. A security camera at the gate was out of service that week. I cannot place {DL} there.\""), .cross("Who had keys to the warehouse?", "\"The owner, {DL}, and a few staff. The contractor also had a gate code for the inspection that day.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Contractor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you close the sprinkler valve?", "\"Yes, for testing. I was running a test on the system and closed it as part of that work.\""), .direct("Did you reopen the valve after testing?", "\"No. I forgot. I got called away, and the valve stayed closed. I feel terrible about that.\""), .direct("Who hired you to do the test?", "\"I was working under a contract, and {D} was the tenant who had asked about the system. My invoice mentions the testing.\""), .direct("What work were you doing at the warehouse?", "\"A scheduled sprinkler test. I closed the control valve to run it and planned to reopen it before leaving.\""), .direct("What happened that afternoon?", "\"I closed the valve around six, ran the flow test, and got called to another job. I left without reopening it.\""), .direct("Did you inform anyone?", "\"No. I meant to call the owner in the morning. I should have left a tag on the valve.\""), .cross("How long was the valve closed before the fire?", "\"About since 6 p.m. I did not check it again, and that was my mistake.\""), .cross("Did you tell anyone the valve was closed?", "\"No. I did not tell the tenant or the owner. I meant to come back and open it.\""), .cross("Did {D} ask you to close the valve?", "\"No. {D.He} did not ask me to close anything. It was part of my testing.\""), .cross("Did the defendant know about the test?", "\"I told the owner I would be there. I did not mention it to {D.him}.\""), .cross("How long did you spend at the site?", "\"About an hour. I left around seven and did not return before the fire.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned a warehouse.", "A contractor."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had closed the sprinkler valve.", "The contractor's invoice mentions testing."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you set the warehouse fire?", "\"No. I did not set it, and I did not close the sprinkler valve. A contractor closed it for testing.\""), .direct("Why did you move stock out days earlier?", "\"It was ordinary. I was reorganizing and moving inventory to a new space, and I did not move it to hide anything.\""), .direct("What does the contractor's invoice show?", "\"That the contractor tested the sprinklers that day. The invoice mentions testing, and that is why the valve was closed.\""), .direct("What do you do with the warehouse space?", "\"I store and ship consumer goods for online sellers. I had leased the warehouse for two years.\""), .direct("Why did you move stock out that week?", "\"I had a new distribution deal in another town and shifted inventory ahead of a larger order. It was planned months earlier.\""), .direct("How did you find out about the fire?", "\"I got a call from the owner around 2 a.m. I raced there and watched it burn.\""), .cross("You removed your stock days before a fire, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I see how that looks. It was a coincidence, and I would not burn a building.\""), .cross("Accelerant was found near the pallets. How do you explain that?", "\"I do not know. I did not put it there. I was not at the warehouse that night.\""), .cross("The valve was closed on the very night of the fire. Is that a coincidence too?", "\"The contractor closed it. I did not know it was closed. I wish I had.\""), .cross("You moved valuable stock out days before a fire. Do you see why that looks suspicious?", "\"I do. But I moved it for a business reason, and I never would have burned a building with my name on the lease.\""), .cross("The sprinklers were off. Who knew how to turn them off?", "\"The contractor did. Any worker with a key could. I did not close the valve and did not know it was closed.\"")],
        openings: ("A warehouse burned with its sprinklers shut off and accelerant near the pallets. {D}, a tenant, had moved stock out days earlier, and the valve was closed at 6 p.m. that night.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that a contractor closed the valve for testing and forgot to reopen it, and that {D}'s move of stock was ordinary business."),
        closings: ("Stock removed days earlier, sprinklers off, accelerant near the pallets, and a building lost. These facts add up to a fire set by someone who knew the building.", "A contractor who closed a valve for testing, admitted forgetting to reopen it, and left a building unprotected. The State has not shown that {D} set the fire."),
        timeline: [(-7, "Stock moves."), (0, "6 p.m.: the valve."), (0, "2 a.m.: the fire."), (0, "3 a.m.: crews.")],
        identified: "A fire report.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let neighborCarGarageBurn = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.neighborCarGarageBurn",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Man Burns Neighbor's Car and Garage Over Fence Dispute", "Gas Can Left in Hedge"],
        law: "burningBuildings",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Willfully and maliciously burned a garage owned by {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A car and detached garage burned on {DATE} after a fence dispute. A gas can was found in a hedge. {D} bought the same can. {DL} says it was stolen.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Fire Report", "Accelerant."), E(.physical, 3, "Gas Can", "In the hedge, {D}'s brand.", .search), E(.video, 2, "Store Camera", "{D} buys a can.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stolen", "{DL} says the can was stolen.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("What did your fire report find?", "\"A car and a detached garage burned after a fence dispute between neighbors. The report found accelerant.\""), .direct("What was found in the hedge?", "\"A gas can, in {D}'s brand. It sat in the hedge near the garage.\""), .direct("What did the store camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} buying a can of the same brand. The camera shows {DL} at the register with it.\""), .direct("What was the state of the garage when crews arrived?", "\"Fully involved, with flames through the roof and the car inside burning. The fire spread to a hedge but was stopped before it reached the house.\""), .direct("Where exactly was the gas can found?", "\"In the hedge about ten feet from the garage door. It still held a small amount of liquid, which tested as gasoline.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the fence dispute?", "\"The neighbors had argued about the property line for months. A deputy had been called once, and each had complained about the other to the city.\""), .cross("{D} says the can was stolen, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} reported the can stolen the week before. I do have a report on file.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant at the garage?", "\"No. No one has placed {D.him} there that night.\""), .cross("Are gas cans of that brand common?", "\"Yes. Many people buy them, and the store sells dozens a week.\""), .cross("Did you find fingerprints on the gas can?", "\"The can was too soot-stained for useful prints. I cannot connect it to a particular hand.\""), .cross("Is that brand sold only at one store?", "\"No. It is sold at several stores and online. The store's camera simply shows {DL} buying one.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Neighbor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you see {D} near the garage that night?", "\"No. I did not see {D}. I was home, and I looked out because of the smoke.\""), .direct("Did you see anyone near the garage?", "\"A car passing by. It went down the road around the time I noticed the glow.\""), .direct("Can you describe that car?", "\"Dark, maybe a sedan. I did not see the plate, and I could not tell who was inside.\""), .direct("How long have you lived on the street?", "\"Eleven years. I know both households and have seen the dispute grow.\""), .direct("What did you see that night?", "\"I looked out around midnight and saw a dark sedan idling down the block with its lights off. A few minutes later I smelled smoke.\""), .direct("Did you see anyone get out?", "\"No. I only saw the car move off slowly. I was not paying close attention until I saw the glow.\""), .cross("How far is your house from the garage?", "\"A few houses down. I could see the garage but not clearly the yard behind it.\""), .cross("Did you hear anything before the fire?", "\"Not that I recall. I only noticed when the light of the fire came through my window.\""), .cross("Do you know about the fence dispute?", "\"Yes. Everyone on the street knew about it. I did not take sides.\""), .cross("Could you see the defendant's house from yours?", "\"Not clearly. It is around a bend. I could see the garage but not {D.his} driveway.\""), .cross("Did you tell deputies about the sedan?", "\"Yes, the next morning. I could not give a plate or a make.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned a garage.", "A stolen can."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had threatened {V} twice.", "{DL} reported the can stolen the week before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you burn the car and garage?", "\"No. I did not set the fire. I would never burn a neighbor's property, even in a dispute.\""), .direct("Whose gas can was in the hedge?", "\"It looks like mine, but it was stolen. I reported it stolen the week before the fire.\""), .direct("What about the threats you made?", "\"I was angry about the fence and I said things. Anger is not a plan, and I did not act on it.\""), .direct("What was the dispute with {V} about?", "\"A fence that ran a foot onto my side. We argued over it for months and traded harsh words.\""), .direct("What did you say to {V} over the fence?", "\"I said things in anger, like that the fence would come down one way or another. I did not mean violence.\""), .direct("How did you find out the can was gone?", "\"The week before, I reached for it in my shed and it was not there. I reported it to deputies right away.\""), .cross("You bought a can of that brand on camera, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I bought one. That is the one that was stolen, and I reported it.\""), .cross("You threatened {V} twice over the fence, didn't you?", "\"I did. I said things in anger. I regret it, but I did not set a fire.\""), .cross("A gas can in your brand was in the hedge by the garage. How is that not you?", "\"Someone took mine and used it. I know how that sounds, but I had already reported it.\""), .cross("You bought that can, and a can of that brand was found at the fire. Why isn't that you?", "\"Because mine was taken. Someone could have used it to point blame at me.\""), .cross("You said the fence would come down 'one way or another.' Doesn't that sound like a threat?", "\"It sounds that way. I was angry, and I meant a lawsuit, not a fire.\"")],
        openings: ("A car and a detached garage burned after a fence dispute. A gas can in {D}'s brand was found in the hedge, a store camera shows {D} buying one, and {D} had threatened the owner twice.", "The defense will present evidence that {D} reported the can stolen the week before the fire and that no one saw {D} near the garage that night."),
        closings: ("A fence dispute, two threats, accelerant, and {D}'s own brand of gas can in the hedge beside the garage. These facts point at {D}.", "A can reported stolen before the fire and no witness near the garage. Anger over a fence is not proof of arson, and the State has not tied {D} to the flame."),
        timeline: [(-7, "The can is reported stolen."), (0, "Midnight: the fire."), (0, "12:30 a.m.: crews."), (1, "The can is found.")],
        identified: "A fire report.",
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "We lost the garage and my truck.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let stillAndGenerators = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.stillAndGenerators",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Deputies Find Moonshine Still and Stolen Generators on Farm", "Barn Wired for Operation"],
        law: "possStolen",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Possessed stolen goods valued at $14,000, knowing them to be stolen, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "Deputies found a moonshine still and six stolen generators in a barn on {DATE}. {D} owns the farm. {DL} says a tenant stored the generators.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Generators", "Six with serials reported stolen.", .search), E(.document, 3, "Deed", "{D} owns the farm."), E(.physical, 2, "Still", "Wired and running.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Tenant", "{DL} says a tenant stored the generators.")],
        role: "Deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Who owns the farm?", "\"{D}. The deed shows {DL} as the owner of the farm and the barn.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you?", "\"That a tenant stored the generators. {DL} said the tenant paid cash rent and used the barn.\""), .direct("How did you come to search the farm?", "\"A tip said stolen generators were on the property. We obtained a warrant and entered the barn at 10 a.m.\""), .direct("What did you find in the barn?", "\"A working still with copper coils and fermenting barrels, plus six generators in the loft. Serial numbers on five matched theft reports from nearby job sites.\""), .direct("What happened with the generators?", "\"We logged them and returned them to their owners after confirming serials. Two other generators had been sold online earlier, according to listings.\""), .direct("What condition was the barn in when you walked through it?", "\"The still was wired and running, and the generators were stacked against a back wall under a tarp. A padlock hung on the main door and the key was on the owner's ring.\""), .cross("Did you find the tenant?", "\"No. We have not found the tenant, only a nickname. I cannot confirm there was one.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant steal the generators?", "\"No. No one saw {DL} take any generator from anywhere.\""), .cross("Was the still on the defendant's land?", "\"Yes. It was in the barn on {D.his} farm.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say anything about the still?", "\"{DL} said it was not {D.his}. {DL} claimed a tenant used the barn.\""), .cross("Were there any signs someone lived in the barn?", "\"A cot, a hot plate, and a few clothes. A person had slept there, but I cannot say who.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Tenant's friend",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did a tenant live on the farm?", "\"Yes. A tenant lived in the barn area and stayed there for some months. I met the tenant a few times.\""), .direct("Do you know the tenant's name?", "\"Only a nickname. I never heard a full name, and I did not ask for one.\""), .direct("How did the tenant pay rent?", "\"In cash, as far as I know. {D} told me the tenant paid cash every month.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"I have known {DF} for several years. I help out on the farm now and then and visit when I am in the area.\""), .direct("What do you know about the tenant?", "\"I met the person once or twice. The person kept to the barn and left at odd hours.\""), .direct("What did you see in the barn?", "\"A cot, boxes, and some equipment. I did not look closely and never saw the back room.\""), .cross("Did you see the still?", "\"No. I did not. I did not go into the back of the barn.\""), .cross("Are you a friend of the tenant?", "\"I know the tenant a little. I am telling you what I saw and nothing beyond it.\""), .cross("Did you ever see generators?", "\"I saw a couple of covered items. I assumed they were farm equipment.\""), .cross("Did you ever talk to the defendant about the tenant?", "\"Briefly. {D.He} said it was a short-term arrangement and left it at that.\""), .cross("Nobody else ever saw the tenant, did they?", "\"I cannot speak for anyone else. I saw a person around the barn a few times, but I never learned a last name or where that person lived.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} held stolen generators.", "A tenant."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold two generators online.", "The tenant paid cash rent."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the generators?", "\"No. I did not steal them. A tenant stored them in my barn, and I did not ask where they came from.\""), .direct("Who was the tenant?", "\"Someone I rented to for cash. I know the person only by a nickname, and I know how that sounds.\""), .direct("Did you sell any of the generators?", "\"I sold two online, as a favor for the tenant. I did not know they were stolen.\""), .direct("How do you use the farm?", "\"I grow hay and keep a few animals. The barn has an old loft and a side room that I rarely use.\""), .direct("How did you meet the tenant?", "\"Through a friend. The person needed storage and a place to stay and paid cash monthly.\""), .direct("What did you do with the two generators you sold?", "\"I posted them online because the tenant asked and gave me a cut. I did not know they were stolen.\""), .cross("You sold two stolen generators online, didn't you?", "\"I sold two. I thought they belonged to the tenant, and I took no cut that I remember.\""), .cross("A running still was in your barn. Whose is that?", "\"It is not mine. I did not know about it. I rarely went into that part of the barn.\""), .cross("You cannot produce the tenant, can you?", "\"No. I do not have a name or address. I know that hurts my case.\""), .cross("You listed two generators online for a tenant you cannot name. Why?", "\"It seemed like an easy favor. I never asked where they came from, and I regret that.\""), .cross("A still ran in your own barn. How could you not know?", "\"I stayed in the house and let the tenant have the barn. I should have checked.\"")],
        openings: ("Deputies found a running moonshine still and six stolen generators in a barn on {D}'s farm. {D} owns the land, and two of the generators were sold online from {D}'s account.", "The defense witnesses will explain that a cash-paying tenant used the barn, that {D} never knew the generators were stolen, and that no one saw {D} take them."),
        closings: ("A still, six stolen generators, two of them sold online, all in a barn that {D} owns. The owner knew what was in that building.", "A tenant who paid cash and used the barn, and an owner who sold two generators as a favor. The State must prove {D} knew they were stolen."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The tenant arrives."), (0, "10 a.m.: the search."), (0, "11 a.m.: serials checked."), (0, "Noon: arrest.")],
        identified: "A search.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"])

    static let scrapYardCopper = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.scrapYardCopper",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Scrap Yard Bought Stolen Power Company Copper", "Weight Tickets Match the Thefts"],
        law: "possStolen",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Possessed stolen copper valued at $31,000, knowing it to be stolen, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A scrap yard owned by {D} bought $31,000 in copper stripped from a power company's yard. Weight tickets matched the thefts. {DL} says sellers gave false names.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Weight Tickets", "Matching weights and dates."), E(.physical, 3, "Copper", "Marked utility copper.", .search), E(.video, 2, "Yard Camera", "Sellers at the scale.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "False Names", "{DL} says sellers gave false names.")],
        role: "Utility security manager",
        exam: [.direct("What did you discover about the copper?", "\"$31,000 in copper had been stripped from our power company yard, and it showed up at {D}'s scrap yard. It was marked utility copper.\""), .direct("How did the weight tickets help?", "\"They matched the dates and weights of the thefts. Each theft lines up with a delivery on a ticket.\""), .direct("How did you discover the theft?", "\"Technicians found stripped transformers and missing copper cable in our storage yard over three weeks. The losses totaled $31,000.\""), .direct("How did you trace the metal?", "\"We asked local scrap yards for weight tickets. One yard's tickets matched our theft dates and weights almost to the pound.\""), .direct("What did the yard camera show?", "\"People weighing in at the scale with loads in pickup beds. The tickets show the same people each week.\""), .direct("What did the company do after the thefts were discovered?", "\"We fenced the yard, added lights and cameras, and compared our inventory to what scrap yards were reporting. The weights and dates lined up with one yard in particular.\""), .cross("{D} says sellers gave false names, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. That can happen at any scrap yard. I will acknowledge that.\""), .cross("Did the defendant report any suspicious sellers?", "\"I understand {DL} reported two sellers to deputies earlier. I will say that is in {DL}'s favor.\""), .cross("Did anyone at the yard know the copper was stolen?", "\"I cannot say. We have the tickets and the copper, not a confession.\""), .cross("Did the defendant buy copper from those same people on other days?", "\"Yes. {D.He} bought from many sellers. We have not examined every ticket.\""), .cross("Was the copper marked as ours?", "\"Some pieces carried stamped markings. Other pieces had been stripped of insulation and could not be identified by sight.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Yard employee",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you check IDs at the scale?", "\"When asked, yes. If a seller seemed unsure, I checked an ID and wrote it on the ticket.\""), .direct("Did you check IDs for every seller?", "\"No, not always. Some sellers were regulars, and we did not ask each time.\""), .direct("How did {D} run the yard?", "\"{D} told us to be careful and to report anything strange. We reported two sellers that I remember.\""), .direct("What do you do at the yard?", "\"I run the scale, record weights, and pay sellers. I have worked there four years.\""), .direct("How did the defendant train you?", "\"To check IDs for new sellers and to report anything strange. {D.He} posted a sign about it at the scale.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the sellers in question?", "\"A few came in with big loads of clean copper and gave names that sounded plain. I did not think they were suspicious.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever tell you to skip the ID check?", "\"I do not recall that. We were just busy, and the check was sometimes skipped.\""), .cross("Were most payments made in cash?", "\"Yes. Most were. Cash is how the yard worked for years.\""), .cross("Did you see the utility markings on the copper?", "\"Sometimes. I did not look hard. Copper looks like copper to me.\""), .cross("Did you check IDs for all of them?", "\"Not always. If a person seemed to be a regular, I did not ask again.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever tell you to skip the check to keep sellers coming?", "\"No. {D.He} never said that. We were just busy, and checks slipped.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} bought stolen copper.", "False names."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} paid cash with no ID checks.", "{DL} reported two sellers to deputies earlier."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you know the copper was stolen?", "\"No. I did not know. I buy scrap every day, and I assumed the sellers owned what they brought.\""), .direct("Did your yard check IDs?", "\"Yes. We checked IDs. Not every time, but we tried. Sellers sometimes gave false names.\""), .direct("Did you ever report suspicious sellers?", "\"Yes. I reported two to deputies earlier. I do not buy stolen goods knowingly.\""), .direct("How long have you owned the yard?", "\"Sixteen years. I buy mixed metals from contractors, farmers, and walk-ins. It is rough work, and we handle tons each week.\""), .direct("How do you deal with sellers?", "\"We weigh, pay, and record names. For copper, we check ID when we remember and photograph the load.\""), .direct("What did you tell deputies?", "\"That the tickets were genuine, that I did not know the copper was stolen, and that the names must have been false.\""), .cross("You paid cash for $31,000 in marked utility copper, didn't you?", "\"Yes. Cash is common in scrap. I did not look at the markings closely.\""), .cross("Your own weight tickets match the thefts, don't they?", "\"They do. That tells me the copper came through my yard, and I am sorry for that.\""), .cross("How do you not notice utility markings on copper?", "\"They are small, and we handle tons.\""), .cross("Cash and no ID checks on $31,000 of copper? Is that how a legitimate yard works?", "\"It is how scrap yards have worked for years. I did check some IDs, but we did not check each one, and that was a mistake.\""), .cross("You reported two sellers to deputies earlier. What does that say?", "\"That I do not want stolen metal. I reported them when something looked off.\"")],
        openings: ("$31,000 in marked copper stripped from a power company yard turned up at a scrap yard owned by {D}. Weight tickets match the dates and weights of the thefts, and cash was paid with few ID checks.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that {D} checked IDs, that sellers gave false names, and that {D} reported two suspicious sellers to deputies before this."),
        closings: ("Marked utility copper, weight tickets that match the thefts, and cash paid at {D}'s scale. A yard owner is responsible for what is bought.", "A scrap yard that checked IDs and reported suspicious sellers. The State must prove {D} knew the copper was stolen, and false names from sellers are not {D}'s knowledge."),
        timeline: [(-30, "Thefts begin."), (0, "Week 4: the tickets."), (0, "Week 4: the search."), (1, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "Weight tickets.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["mistakeOfFact"])

    static let poisonedNeighborDogs = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.poisonedNeighborDogs",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Man Poisons Neighbor's Dogs Over Barking", "Antifreeze in Meat Scraps"],
        law: "animalCruelty",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Maliciously killed animals belonging to {V} by poison, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Two dogs died on {DATE} after eating meat scraps laced with antifreeze thrown over a fence. {D}, a neighbor, had complained about barking. {DL} says a stranger did it.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Necropsy", "Antifreeze poisoning."), E(.video, 2, "Yard Camera", "A figure at the fence."), E(.physical, 3, "Scraps", "Meat with antifreeze in {D}'s trash.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stranger", "{DL} says a stranger did it.")],
        role: "Veterinarian",
        exam: [.direct("What did your necropsy show?", "\"Antifreeze poisoning in both dogs. They died after eating meat scraps that had been laced with it.\""), .direct("How did the dogs get the scraps?", "\"Someone threw them over the fence. The yard camera shows a figure at the fence.\""), .direct("What did deputies find in {D}'s trash?", "\"Meat scraps with antifreeze on them. {D} is a neighbor who had complained about the barking.\""), .direct("What symptoms did the dogs show when brought to you?", "\"Vomiting, stumbling, and weakness within a few hours. Both dogs had very low blood chemistry and kidney failure consistent with ethylene glycol.\""), .direct("What did you tell the owners?", "\"That the dogs had been poisoned and that the prognosis was grim. We tried supportive care, but both died during the night.\""), .direct("What did you find in the stomach contents?", "\"Chunks of cooked meat mixed with a sweet-smelling green liquid. Lab tests confirmed antifreeze.\""), .cross("{D}'s trash was open to the street, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, I understand it was often open. Anyone could have put scraps in it.\""), .cross("Did a jug of antifreeze turn up at {D}'s home?", "\"Yes. A jug in the garage. Many people keep one for cars.\""), .cross("Can you tell who threw the scraps?", "\"No. I can tell you what killed the dogs. I cannot say who threw it.\""), .cross("How common is antifreeze poisoning in dogs?", "\"Fairly common. It is sweet, and dogs will lap it from driveways or garages. Intentional cases are rarer.\""), .cross("Can you tell how long the meat sat before the dogs ate it?", "\"No. The scraps could have been placed minutes before or hours before.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Neighbor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Is {D}'s trash often left open?", "\"Often. I see it open to the street most weeks. Raccoons and strays get into it.\""), .direct("Was the trash open on the day the dogs died?", "\"I am not sure. I did not look that day, but it is usually open.\""), .direct("Do you know the defendant to be cruel to animals?", "\"No. I have never seen that. {D} complained about barking but never struck me as cruel.\""), .direct("How long have you lived near the defendant?", "\"Nine years. I see {D.his} trash and yard every day when I walk my own dog.\""), .direct("What is the defendant's trash routine?", "\"Cans left near the curb with the lid half off. Stray animals get into it often, and I have chased cats out of it.\""), .direct("What kind of neighbor is the defendant?", "\"Quiet, cranky about noise, but not violent. I never saw {DF} mistreat an animal.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} near the fence that day?", "\"No. I did not see {D.him}. I was not home during the afternoon.\""), .cross("Did the defendant complain about the dogs to you?", "\"Yes. {D.He} complained about the barking a few times. We all did.\""), .cross("Could someone else have put scraps in the trash?", "\"Yes. It was open to the street. Anyone passing could have.\""), .cross("Were you home that afternoon?", "\"Not for most of it. I was at work and came home after six.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone throw anything over the fence?", "\"No. I did not see anyone. I only know what neighbors told me afterward.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} poisoned dogs.", "A stranger."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a jug of antifreeze in the garage.", "{DL}'s trash was open to the street."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you poison the dogs?", "\"No. I did not poison anyone's dogs. I would never do that, even though the barking bothered me.\""), .direct("How did scraps with antifreeze get into your trash?", "\"My trash is open to the street. Someone else put them there, after throwing them over the fence.\""), .direct("Why do you have a jug of antifreeze?", "\"For my car. I keep it in the garage, like many people do. It was not used for that.\""), .direct("How long have you lived next to the dogs?", "\"Six years. They bark at night and early in the morning, and I have complained to the owners several times.\""), .direct("What happened that afternoon?", "\"I was at work most of the day. I came home around six and sat on my porch. I heard the dogs barking and later heard they had died.\""), .direct("How did you learn about the scraps in your trash?", "\"Deputies searched the can after the necropsy and found some meat with a green stain. I was shocked.\""), .cross("You complained about the barking, didn't you?", "\"Yes. Many times. But complaining is not poisoning.\""), .cross("The antifreeze was in your garage and the scraps in your trash, weren't they?", "\"Yes. I see the pattern, but it was a setup or a coincidence. I did not do it.\""), .cross("Two dogs are dead. Who do you think did it?", "\"I do not know. A stranger, maybe. I am sorry for the owners.\""), .cross("You have a jug of antifreeze in your garage. Who else has access?", "\"Anyone who walks in. I leave the garage door open often. A jug on a shelf is not unusual.\""), .cross("You complained about the barking more than once. Isn't that a motive?", "\"It would be a motive for a different kind of person. I do not hurt animals.\"")],
        openings: ("Two dogs died after eating meat scraps laced with antifreeze thrown over a fence. A camera shows a figure at the fence, and scraps with antifreeze were found in the trash of {D}, who had complained about the barking.", "The defense case is that {D}'s trash was open to the street, that antifreeze is common, and that no one saw {D} throw anything."),
        closings: ("Two poisoned dogs, a figure at the fence, a complaint about barking, and scraps with antifreeze in {D}'s trash and a jug in the garage. The evidence is all on one side.", "An open trash can, a common product, and a figure whose face no one saw. The State has not shown that {D} was at that fence."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The complaints."), (0, "6 p.m.: scraps thrown."), (0, "9 p.m.: the dogs fall ill."), (0, "Midnight: they die.")],
        identified: "A necropsy.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "They were my kids' dogs.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let puppyMillCrates = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.puppyMillCrates",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Breeder Kept Forty Dogs in Filthy Crates Without Water", "Deputies Remove Animals in Hazmat Suits"],
        law: "animalCruelty",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Intentionally deprived animals of necessary sustenance and care, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "Deputies found forty dogs in stacked crates without water in a barn on {DATE}. Six were dying. {D} owns the barn. {DL} says a helper was feeding them.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Barn Condition", "Stacked crates; empty bowls.", .search), E(.forensic, 3, "Veterinary Reports", "Dehydration in twenty-two dogs."), E(.document, 2, "Sales Records", "{D}'s sales.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Helper", "{DL} says a helper fed them.")],
        role: "Animal control officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find in the barn?", "\"Forty dogs in stacked crates, with empty water bowls. Six were dying when we arrived.\""), .direct("What did the veterinary reports show?", "\"Dehydration in twenty-two dogs. Several were in critical condition and needed immediate care.\""), .direct("Whose barn is it?", "\"{D}'s. The sales records show {DL} selling puppies, and {D.he} had advertised puppies that very week.\""), .direct("How did you learn of the barn?", "\"A caller reported a terrible smell and constant whining from a barn on a rural lot. We went with a veterinarian and a deputy that morning.\""), .direct("What was the condition inside?", "\"Forty dogs in stacked wire crates, urine-soaked floors, and empty water bowls. Six were lethargic and nearly unresponsive, and many had sunken eyes.\""), .direct("What did you do for the animals?", "\"We removed them by 3 p.m. and drove them to a shelter. A veterinarian examined each, treated twenty-two for dehydration, and euthanized two that could not recover.\""), .cross("{D} says a helper was feeding them, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. A helper fed the dogs until quitting about three days earlier.\""), .cross("How long had the dogs been without water?", "\"Several days, based on the veterinary findings. Three days fits what we saw.\""), .cross("Did the defendant cooperate when you arrived?", "\"Yes. {D.He} let us in and did not interfere. I will say that.\""), .cross("Could the dogs have gone without water for only a day?", "\"Not with that level of dehydration. The veterinarian's findings suggest at least two to three days.\""), .cross("Were there any food bowls or supplies in the barn?", "\"Yes, a few. Dog food bags were stacked by the door. The water source was a spigot on the far wall, and the hose was disconnected.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Former helper",
