        role: "Wildlife officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see in the video?", "\"It shows {D} filming a bear cub being struck. The video was posted to a group by {DL}'s account.\""), .direct("What did the necropsy find?", "\"Injuries consistent with blows. The cub died from the injuries.\""), .direct("How was {DL} connected?", "\"{DL} appears in the video and the account that posted it is {DL}'s.\""), .direct("How did your office learn of the video?", "\"A tip from a viewer who recognized the setting. We obtained the file from the account that posted it and preserved the original.\""), .direct("What does the video show in detail?", "\"A small bear cub on a dirt road. A person kicks and hits the cub with a stick while the camera follows closely, and laughing can be heard behind it.\""), .direct("What was the result of the necropsy?", "\"Multiple fractures consistent with blows and internal bleeding. The cub would have been unable to survive without care.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} was only recording, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"The video shows another person striking. But {D.he} filmed and posted it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} strike the cub?", "\"Not as far as the video shows. Another person did.\""), .cross("Is filming a crime?", "\"Not by itself. But {D.he} encouraged it, according to others, and posted it.\""), .cross("Whose voice is behind the camera?", "\"The audio matches {D.his} voice from other posts. It is clear enough to hear commentary, but I cannot decode every word.\""), .cross("Does the video show {D} touching the cub?", "\"No. The person doing the striking is a second individual, not {DL}.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Hunting club member",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you hunt with {DL}?", "\"Yes. We're in the same hunting club. I know {D} well.\""), .direct("Was {DL} the one who struck?", "\"No. {D.He} didn't strike. The other person did.\""), .direct("What did {DL} do?", "\"Filmed. {D.He} was recording.\""), .direct("How long have you been in the club?", "\"Nine years. We hunt, fish, and do some conservation work. {D.He} has been a member for about five.\""), .direct("What kind of member is {D}?", "\"Reliable on work days, though a little too eager to be liked by the other members. {D.He} has never been in trouble with the club before this.\""), .direct("What did you think when you saw the video?", "\"I felt sick watching it. I messaged {D.him} that night and said it was wrong, and {D.he} apologized and took the video down.\""), .cross("Did {DL} egg on the other person?", "\"Yes. {D.He} cheered and laughed. I saw that.\""), .cross("Did {DL} stop it?", "\"Not right away. I'm not sure {DF} stopped it.\""), .cross("Do you approve of it?", "\"No. It was wrong. I'm telling what I saw.\""), .cross("Did the defendant encourage the other person?", "\"On the video, yes. I heard cheering and laughter. I do not defend that.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant step in to stop it?", "\"No. I was not there when it happened, and the video itself does not show {DF} trying to stop it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} joined in torturing a cub.", "Only recording."),
        allocution: "\"It was a stupid thing.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} laughed and egged on the other man.", "{DL} told the other man to stop once."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you filming?", "\"I was recording what the other person was doing. I wasn't striking anything. I was just there.\""), .direct("Why did you post it?", "\"I thought it would be funny. I didn't think about the cruelty. I regret posting it.\""), .direct("Did you tell them to stop?", "\"I may have said something. I didn't stop it. I should have.\""), .direct("How did you know the other person?", "\"A friend from the hunting club. We were out in the woods when we came across the cub on the road.\""), .direct("What did you do with your phone?", "\"I started recording on instinct. I thought it would be a funny clip to share with other members.\""), .direct("What did you do after the video was over?", "\"I posted it that night. By the next morning I regretted it and took it down, but it had already spread.\""), .cross("You filmed a cub being struck, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. It was wrong.\""), .cross("You posted the video, didn't you?", "\"Yes. From my account. I'm ashamed.\""), .cross("You laughed, didn't you?", "\"I did. I'm not proud. I thought it was a joke.\""), .cross("You could have put the camera down and stopped it. Why didn't you?", "\"I froze, and honestly I was going along with it. I should have stepped in.\""), .cross("The audio has you laughing. What was funny about it?", "\"Nothing. I was nervous and laughed without thinking. It was not funny, and I am deeply sorry.\"")],
        openings: ("A video shows a bear cub being struck, filmed and posted by {D}. A necropsy found injuries consistent with blows. The State will present the wildlife officer and the video.", "The defense will present a person who did not strike the cub and only recorded, and who now regrets it. Listen closely to the witnesses."),
        closings: ("A cub beaten to death on camera, with {D} filming, laughing, and posting the video for others to see. The law punishes those who help and encourage cruelty, not just those who strike the blow.", "{D} did not strike the cub and was only holding a phone when the other person acted. The State has not proved that {D} meant to aid in the cruelty or that filming alone makes {D} a participant."),
